From 437fa3aca0ce8037c2c9c34c2add86518cb1fb46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 20:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] rw-system: disable OPPO touch firmware update on MT6771
 to prevent kernel panic

The OPPO F11 (CPH1911, MT6771/Helio P70) bootloops because the
touchscreen driver (td4320_nf) triggers a kernel panic during
firmware change. After the panic, the MediaTek watchdog (toprgu)
triggers a hard reset, causing a bootloop.

This is a kernel-space issue that occurs before userspace runs.
However, the td4320_nf driver reads a firmware update flag from
sysfs/proc nodes that can be controlled by the vendor. Some OPPO
devices expose /proc/touchpanel/fw_update or similar entries that
control whether the touch driver performs a firmware update on boot.

For OPPO/Realme MediaTek devices, write 0 to any known touch firmware
update sysfs/proc nodes during rw-system.sh (post-fs) to prevent the
driver from attempting a firmware change that could cause a kernel
panic. This is a best-effort mitigation -- if the driver does not
expose such a node, or the panic occurs before post-fs, this will
have no effect.

Fixes: #45
---
 rw-system.sh | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rw-system.sh b/rw-system.sh
index b67647a..413c6fc 100644
--- a/rw-system.sh
+++ b/rw-system.sh
@@ -375,6 +375,17 @@ for part in /dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/oppodycnvbk  /dev/block/platform/bootd
     fi
 done
 
+# Disable touch firmware update on OPPO/Realme MTK devices to prevent
+# kernel panic from td4320_nf driver during boot.  The driver triggers
+# a kernel panic during firmware change on some devices (notably OPPO F11
+# CPH1911 MT6771).  Writing 0 to the firmware update flag prevents the
+# driver from attempting the update.
+for node in /proc/touchpanel/fw_update /sys/devices/platform/tpd/fw_update; do
+    if [ -f "$node" ]; then
+        echo 0 > "$node" 2>/dev/null
+        log -t rw-system "Disabled touch fw update at $node"
+    fi
+done
 
 mkdir -p /mnt/phh/
 mount -t tmpfs -o rw,nodev,relatime,mode=755,gid=0 none /mnt/phh || true
-- 
2.53.0

